mov/hls: seeking in HLS streams made of fragmented MP4 segments lands where asked.

Third modification VideoFun makes to FFmpeg 6.1.1 (LGPL-2.1+; this patch is under the same
licence). hls_read_seek() resets the input position to 0 to tell the subdemuxer it has seeked;
mpegts handles that, but 6.1's mov demuxer kept the pre-seek fragment index and sample cursors,
so after a seek in an HLS stream made of fMP4 segments it read the re-fetched init and target
segment as the remainder of the previous mdat and returned no packets until EOF. When the
position is 0 the fragment index and every stream's index entries and sample cursor are now
discarded and the next root atom is searched with mov_switch_root(s, -1, -1), which (as in
master) now reads on from the current position when given no target. Backported from
FFmpeg master (patch by vectronic, FFmpeg ticket 7359), adapted to 6.1 field names
(ctts_index / ctts_sample).

hls.c (VideoFun's own change, not upstream): after a seek, packets are discarded until one at or
after the segment start; that test used dts, so the keyframe opening a segment with B-frames (dts a
frame before its pts) was discarded and the seek landed up to a GOP late. The test now uses pts
when present.

--- a/libavformat/hls.c	2026-10-18 20:29:50
+++ b/libavformat/hls.c	2026-10-18 20:29:50
@@ -2336,8 +2336,13 @@
                     }
 
                     tb = get_timebase(pls);
-                    ts_diff = av_rescale_rnd(pls->pkt->dts, AV_TIME_BASE,
-                                            tb.den, AV_ROUND_DOWN) -
+                    /* Judge the packet by its PRESENTATION time when it has one: a keyframe
+                     * that opens a segment with B-frames has its dts a frame or two before the
+                     * segment start, so the dts test discarded it and the seek landed a whole GOP
+                     * late (VideoFun #67: 10.5 s -> first picture at 14.2 s). */
+                    ts_diff = av_rescale_rnd(pls->pkt->pts != AV_NOPTS_VALUE ? pls->pkt->pts
+                                                                           : pls->pkt->dts,
+                                            AV_TIME_BASE, tb.den, AV_ROUND_DOWN) -
                             pls->seek_timestamp;
                     if (ts_diff >= 0 && (pls->seek_flags  & AVSEEK_FLAG_ANY ||
                                         pls->pkt->flags & AV_PKT_FLAG_KEY)) {
